TEST: wifi: ath11k: add a tso switch for A/B tests

Test only, dropped before this is upstreamed. Add the module parameter
tso (bool, 0644, default on). At load it decides whether the netdevs
offer scatter-gather, TSO and frame lists; for each frame, off sends a
TCP batch segmented in software and a frame with fragments made linear,
as the stack would, so both paths can be compared in one boot.

The test image also starts with the receive merge (rx_merge) and the
switches of the changes new in it off (rx_refill_chunk, txq_wake_check,
rx_merge_egress, rx_buf_join, rx_sync_buf, rx_merge_fwd, tx_seg_count,
dp_irq_spread), so that a fault in one cannot crash-loop the router; the
bench turns them on after boot (dp_irq_spread as a module option).

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
